# 🔹 Differences: Array Stack vs Linked List Stack
| Feature               | Array-based Stack         | Linked List Stack |
|------------------------|---------------------------|-------------------|
| Size Limit             | Fixed (`MAXSIZE`)         | Dynamic (no fixed size) |
| Memory Usage           | Pre-allocated             | Allocated per node |
| Implementation         | Simple, faster            | Slightly more complex |
| Overflow Condition     | When array is full        | When heap memory exhausted |
| Underflow Condition    | When `top == -1`          | When `top == NULL` |

